{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB06691 - MONDO_6004",
  "verbalization": "Mepyramine, a selective alpha-1 adrenergic receptor antagonist, is implicated in the pathogenesis of Vasomotor Rhinitis through a series of interconnected indications. The evidence suggests that Mepyramine may exert its therapeutic effects on Vasomotor Rhinitis via the modulation of inflammatory and vascular responses. Specifically, Mepyramine is associated with Nasopharyngitis and Tramazoline, both of which are linked to Vasomotor Rhinitis, indicating a potential pathway involving inflammatory mediators and vascular dysfunction. Additionally, Mepyramine's association with Allergic Rhinitis and Isoflupredone Acetate further supports a mechanism involving inflammatory pathways, as Isoflupredone Acetate is a known mediator in allergic rhinitis. The integrated evidence suggests that Mepyramine may modulate vascular tone and inflammatory responses, potentially alleviating symptoms of Vasomotor Rhinitis. The strength of the evidence is supported by the consistent clinical indications across multiple paths, though the exact mechanism remains partially elucidated, requiring further experimental validation.",
